 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Hydrolyzes UDP-glucose to glucose 1-phosphate and UMPand ADP-ribose to ribose 5-phosphate and AMP. The physiologicalsubstrate is probably UDP-glucose. Poor activity on othersubstrates such as ADP-glucose, CDP-glucose, GDP-glucose and GDP-mannose.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=UDP-sugar + H(2)O = UMP + alpha-D-aldose 1-phosphate.;EC=3.6.1.45;COFACTOR:Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:pH dependence:Optimum pH is 8.0-9.5.;SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12429023}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12429023}.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the Nudix hydrolase family. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=AAD15563.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_14847_identity</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

