<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P50053">
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ketohexokinase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P50053" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_KHK_identity" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KHK_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.7.1.3</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Hepatic fructokinase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KHK</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">KHK_HUMAN Reviewed; 298 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Catalyzes the phosphorylation of the ketose sugarfructose to fructose-1-phosphate. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941785}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=ATP + beta-D-fructose = ADP + beta-D-fructose 1-phosphate+ H(+); Xref=Rhea:RHEA:18145, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:28645, ChEBI:CHEBI:30616, ChEBI:CHEBI:138881,ChEBI:CHEBI:456216; EC=2.7.1.3;Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941785};ACTIVITY REGULATION: Requires potassium. Inhibition by ADP.BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=0.8 mM for D-fructose (at 25 degrees Celsius){ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941785};KM=0.15 mM for Mg-ATP (at 25 degrees Celsius){ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941785};Note=kcat is 7.6 sec(-1). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941785};PATHWAY: Carbohydrate metabolism; fructose metabolism.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19237742}.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=C {ECO:0000269|PubMed:9799106}; Synonyms=Central,hepatic/renal/intestinal {ECO:0000269|PubMed:9799106};IsoId=P50053-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=A {ECO:0000269|PubMed:9799106}; Synonyms=Peripheral{ECO:0000269|PubMed:9799106};IsoId=P50053-2; Sequence=VSP_004669;Note=More widely distributed but with a low expression level.KM=7 mM for D-fructose (at 25 degrees Celsius). KM=036 mM forMg-ATP (at 25 degrees Celsius). kcat is 6.9 sec(-1).{ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941785};TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Most abundant in liver, kidney, gut, spleenand pancreas. Low levels also found in adrenal, muscle, brain andeye. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:9799106}.DISEASE: Fructosuria (FRUCT) [MIM:229800]: Benign defect ofintermediary metabolism. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12941785,ECO:0000269|PubMed:7833921}. Note=The disease is caused bymutations affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the carbohydrate kinase PfkB family.{ECO:0000305}. COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
